From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:24:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 280/333] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on the queued
 Compact safe point

Review fixes to the previous patch (2026-11-01).

The prepare turn is now the session running while this plan's prepare
message is in the transcript. With background shells no longer holding the
plan back, an unrelated turn (a shell's task notification, a scheduled
prompt, a sub-agent hand-back) that ran while the prepare send was in flight
or buffered by the runner set sawTurn, the failure check fell back to the
send-time snapshot, and the plan compacted before the notes were saved. The
anchor is the committed user_message block that lands on
session_input_consumed; a prepare message already in the transcript at send
time (an earlier compact's) is skipped by object and server item id.
Failure is judged only on blocks after the anchor, and the snapshot
fallback is removed. Any running edge still keeps the 30 s start timer from
failing the plan, since the prepare message may wait behind another turn;
the 15 minute limit ends a plan whose message never lands.

Correction to the previous patch's wording: on this pin the server rewrites
a non-codex `waiting` with a background task count to `idle`, so the cause
was the sticky shell count on `idle`, not a `waiting` turn end. `waiting` is
accepted for parity with maybeFlushQueuedHead. The reducer-driven tests now
end turns as `idle` with a shell count, keep one `waiting` compatibility
case (SDK orchestrators parked on sub-agents, codex-native children), and
add cases for a turn that runs before the prepare message lands, a prepare
message left by an earlier compact, and one that never lands. A comment by
the compact call notes that Claude Code queues a /compact typed while a
shell wakes the chat into a new turn.
